# Auto-detect text files and normalize line endings to LF.
#
# Scoped to components/zenoh_pico on purpose:
#   - zenoh-pico/ is a trimmed copy of upstream zenoh-pico 1.9.0, and VENDOR.md
#     promises it is byte-for-byte unmodified. Upstream is LF.
#   - include/ and src/ are LuatOS glue code, also LF.
# The tree was first added from a Windows working copy, so every vendored file
# landed as CRLF (upstream bytes + one CR per line). These rules keep the whole
# component LF so the copy stays byte-identical to upstream.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Source files - enforce LF
*.c     text eol=lf
*.h     text eol=lf
*.lua   text eol=lf
*.py    text eol=lf
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf
*.cmake text eol=lf
Makefile text eol=lf
